WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:16.400
was tired after their rapid zapping to reach the mines.

2
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.381
But he felt relieved to be back in the vortex.

3
00:00:20.102 --> 00:00:22.723
"I know Perda didn't want to leave Mellis," he thought.

4
00:00:22.743 --> 00:00:23.884
"I didn't either.

5
00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.226
But my parents and Boz can help her better than we can."

6
00:00:27.246 --> 00:00:31.048
"I wish we knew how to go straight back to Magica," he said.

7
00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:34.370
"We might need to stop and rest in the first safe world we find."

8
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.311
"Yes." Perda sounded distracted.

9
00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:41.253
"Hey, Zann, did you notice the vortex looks familiar?"

10
00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:43.575
Zann laughed.

11
00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:45.876
"Of course it does!

12
00:00:46.456 --> 00:00:48.157
We've been through it lots of times."

13
00:00:48.998 --> 00:00:51.179
"No, that's not what I mean," Perda said.

14
00:00:51.199 --> 00:00:55.241
"Remember how strange it was when we were on our way to Terrica?

15
00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:58.063
Now it looks just like it usually does."

16
00:00:58.903 --> 00:01:00.444
Zann realized she was right.

17
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.702
"I hadn't even noticed," he said.

18
00:01:02.722 --> 00:01:05.964
"I was just glad to be away from Zira and her goons!

19
00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:07.305
But you're right.

20
00:01:07.886 --> 00:01:08.827
Not that it matters though.

21
00:01:09.507 --> 00:01:10.328
We're on our way home."

22
00:01:11.229 --> 00:01:14.471
He couldn't imagine how worried their families must be by now.

23
00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:18.755
Still, he knew they had to rest to regain their magic energy.

24
00:01:19.295 --> 00:01:21.277
Otherwise the vortex wouldn't be safe.

25
00:01:22.238 --> 00:01:26.521
"Sort of like it wasn't safe for the miner I accidentally pushed in," Zann thought.

26
00:01:27.022 --> 00:01:29.244
Would he ever stop feeling guilty about that?

27
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.843
He tried not to think about it as he grabbed a passing wormhole.

28
00:01:33.643 --> 00:01:38.367
He pulled himself partway through so that he and Perda could see the world on the other side.

29
00:01:38.928 --> 00:01:43.372
It was barren and dark, with no sign of people and hardly any plants.

30
00:01:43.392 --> 00:01:46.174
"This isn't Fardark again, is it?"

31
00:01:46.494 --> 00:01:47.735
Perda sounded uneasy.

32
00:01:47.755 --> 00:01:52.519
"There's no lightning or monsters around, so probably not," Zann said.

33
00:01:52.539 --> 00:01:54.541
"But let's keep going just in case.

34
00:01:55.222 --> 00:01:57.844
We still have enough energy to find a better world to rest in.

35
00:01:58.408 --> 00:01:59.990
Or maybe we'll find Magica next."

36
00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:05.734
"Maybe," Perda said as they let go of the wormhole and tumbled on through the vortex.

37
00:02:05.754 --> 00:02:10.178
"But right now I'd settle for any friendly, peaceful world.

38
00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:15.943
Especially if it's a familiar one like Pax or Rood or maybe Niffia!"

39
00:02:15.963 --> 00:02:19.586
"Niffia?" Zann laughed.

40
00:02:20.207 --> 00:02:23.169
"You must be desperate if you want to find that stinky place!"

41
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.992
They grabbed another wormhole and looked out.

42
00:02:26.924 --> 00:02:30.867
But this world was overcast, with lightning flashing between the clouds.

43
00:02:31.748 --> 00:02:32.528
Zann shuddered.

44
00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:35.730
"Okay, this world definitely looks like Fardark.

45
00:02:36.451 --> 00:02:39.033
At least, it's similar enough that I don't want to take a chance."

46
00:02:39.053 --> 00:02:41.174
"I agree," Perda said.

47
00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.916
"It's a good thing the vortex is back to normal.

48
00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:48.339
It's not sapping our energy as fast as it did on the way to Terrica."

49
00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.801
They tried a third wormhole.

50
00:02:51.682 --> 00:02:54.644
It showed a barren, rocky world with tall mountains.

51
00:02:55.244 --> 00:02:56.945
But the sky was bright and clear.

52
00:02:57.566 --> 00:03:00.428
Zann spotted a man wandering around in the distance.

53
00:03:00.448 --> 00:03:02.149
"Look, there's a person!"

54
00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:02.829
he said.

55
00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.050
"Let's stop here.

56
00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.132
Maybe that guy can help us figure out how to find Magica."

57
00:03:07.152 --> 00:03:10.494
"I don't recognize this world," Perda said.

58
00:03:10.514 --> 00:03:15.738
"It doesn't look much more pleasant than the last two, but I suppose it will have to do."

59
00:03:16.578 --> 00:03:19.140
They pulled themselves out and onto the rocky ground.

60
00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.083
Perda undid their shackles, and they hurried toward the man.

61
00:03:23.983 --> 00:03:27.345
His back was to them, but he heard them coming and spun around.

62
00:03:28.006 --> 00:03:29.527
His face looked terrified.

63
00:03:30.147 --> 00:03:31.608
It also looked familiar.

64
00:03:32.289 --> 00:03:33.109
Zann gasped.

65
00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:34.330
"It's you!"

66
00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.852
he blurted out as he recognized the miner from Terrica.

67
00:03:38.613 --> 00:03:39.854
The miner stared at him.

68
00:03:39.874 --> 00:03:42.435
"Yes, it's me, Yarb."

69
00:03:43.236 --> 00:03:44.757
Then he glanced around.

70
00:03:44.777 --> 00:03:46.278
"How did you get here?

71
00:03:46.598 --> 00:03:47.839
This place is dangerous!"

72
00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.841
A large shadow passed overhead.

73
00:03:51.621 --> 00:03:53.883
Perda glanced up and gasped with fear.

74
00:03:55.424 --> 00:03:58.106
"Zann, I recognize that species from your parents' book.

75
00:03:58.747 --> 00:03:59.948
I think we're in Drac!

76
00:04:00.649 --> 00:04:03.071
It's the only world the species lives in."

77
00:04:03.091 --> 00:04:06.213
"We have to get out of here," Zann told Yarb.

78
00:04:06.794 --> 00:04:08.695
"Dragons eat people in this world!"

79
00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.117
"Dragons?" Yarb said.

80
00:04:11.137 --> 00:04:12.659
"Is that what they're called?

81
00:04:13.339 --> 00:04:14.881
They keep trying to attack me!"

82
00:04:15.481 --> 00:04:20.385
Zann shackled their arms together while Perda grabbed Zing and shackled herself to Zann.

83
00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:23.388
Then they all sprinted back to the wormhole.

84
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.681
The dragon dived toward them.

85
00:04:26.482 --> 00:04:30.825
A burst of flame shot out, but they leaped into the wormhole before it reached them.

86
00:04:32.226 --> 00:04:34.927
Soon they were tumbling through the vortex again.

87
00:04:34.947 --> 00:04:38.830
"I can't believe we found you," Zann said to Yarb.

88
00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:44.274
"Perda, this is the guy I was telling you about—the miner I accidentally pushed into that wormhole."

89
00:04:44.294 --> 00:04:46.896
"Wormhole?" Yarb said.

90
00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:48.477
"I don't understand."

91
00:04:48.497 --> 00:04:51.559
"I'm really sorry," Zann said.

92
00:04:51.579 --> 00:04:53.120
"I didn't mean to do it."

93
00:04:54.208 --> 00:04:57.489
He quickly explained what had happened and how the vortex worked.

94
00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:00.591
"You don't need to apologize," Yarb said.

95
00:05:00.611 --> 00:05:02.812
"I was wrong to attack you.

96
00:05:03.312 --> 00:05:04.593
And I got what I deserved."

97
00:05:05.353 --> 00:05:05.893
He shuddered.

98
00:05:06.393 --> 00:05:07.874
"That world was terrifying!"

99
00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.695
Feelings of relief swept over Zann.

100
00:05:11.235 --> 00:05:14.017
"I was so worried that I'd killed him," he thought.

101
00:05:14.037 --> 00:05:16.378
"And I'm glad he's not mad!"

102
00:05:16.398 --> 00:05:19.139
"Let's find another world," Perda said.

103
00:05:19.159 --> 00:05:21.440
"We all need to rest."

104
00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.161
Yarb looked amazed.

105
00:05:24.641 --> 00:05:26.102
"How many worlds are there?"

106
00:05:26.923 --> 00:05:28.224
Zann gave a short laugh.

107
00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:31.086
"Lots!" "Okay.

108
00:05:31.466 --> 00:05:33.027
There's another wormhole coming up."

109
00:05:33.787 --> 00:05:35.689
Perda reached out and grabbed the edge.

110
00:05:36.449 --> 00:05:38.411
When they looked out, they saw a beach.

111
00:05:39.151 --> 00:05:42.213
In one direction lay a lush, dripping forest.

112
00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:47.176
In the other was the sea, its waves rolling over the sandy shore.

113
00:05:47.777 --> 00:05:48.877
A gentle rain fell.

114
00:05:48.898 --> 00:05:52.360
"It looks pretty damp out there," Perda commented.

115
00:05:52.948 --> 00:05:54.289
"Maybe it's Mistafar."

116
00:05:55.189 --> 00:05:56.710
Zann felt a flare of hope.

117
00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:02.172
If Perda's guess was right, their friend Ello's people would be able to help them return home.

118
00:06:02.852 --> 00:06:04.873
They pulled themselves out and onto the beach.

119
00:06:05.413 --> 00:06:10.435
When Zann looked toward the sea, he noticed something bobbing along in the surf nearby.

120
00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:13.956
He squinted, trying to get a better look through the drizzle.

121
00:06:13.976 --> 00:06:15.977
"Hey, look at that," he said.

122
00:06:15.997 --> 00:06:18.418
"Am I so tired that I'm seeing things?

123
00:06:19.279 --> 00:06:21.980
Or does that look like a gulper heading this way?"
